# Smart Neighborhood Reporting App – Walkthrough

## What Was Built

A complete **Flutter + Firebase MVP** with 8 screens, 3 services, and 2 models, ready to connect to Firebase.

### Project Structure

```
lib/
├── main.dart                          ← Firebase init + theme + routes
├── firebase_options.dart              ← YOU generate this (see below)
├── models/
│   ├── user_model.dart                ← uid, name, email, role
│   └── report_model.dart             ← Reports with Timestamp
├── services/
│   ├── auth_service.dart              ← register, login, logout, getRole
│   ├── report_service.dart            ← CRUD + real-time streams
│   └── storage_service.dart           ← Image upload
└── screens/
    ├── splash_screen.dart             ← Animated splash + auth check
    ├── login_screen.dart              ← Glassmorphism login
    ├── register_screen.dart           ← Registration form
    ├── home_screen.dart               ← Stream-based report list
    ├── create_report_screen.dart      ← Image + GPS + submit
    ├── report_details_screen.dart     ← SliverAppBar + admin actions
    ├── admin_home_screen.dart         ← Stats + filter + manage
    └── profile_screen.dart            ← User info + logout
```

---

## 🔥 Firebase Setup (Required Before Running)

### Step 1: Install Firebase CLI
```bash
npm install -g firebase-tools
firebase login
```

### Step 2: Install FlutterFire CLI
```bash
dart pub global activate flutterfire_cli
```

### Step 3: Create Firebase Project
1. Go to [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com)
2. Create a new project (e.g., `smart-neighborhood`)
3. Enable **Authentication** → Email/Password
4. Enable **Cloud Firestore** (start in test mode)
5. Enable **Storage** (start in test mode)

### Step 4: Configure Flutter Project
```bash
cd f:\Smart_Neighborhood_Reporting_App
flutterfire configure
```
This generates `lib/firebase_options.dart` automatically.

### Step 5: Install Dependencies & Run
```bash
flutter pub get
flutter run
```

---

## 🧪 Testing Flow

1. **Register** a new user → creates `users` doc with `role: "user"`
2. **Login** → navigates to Home screen
3. **Create Report** → pick image + get GPS + submit
4. **View Reports** → real-time list with filters
5. **Make user admin:** In Firebase Console → Firestore → `users` → open user doc → change `role` to `admin`
6. **Login as admin** → see Admin Dashboard with stats
7. **Change status** to Resolved → badge turns green
8. **Delete report** → confirm dialog → removed

---

## 🎨 Design Highlights

| Feature | Details |
|---|---|
| **Theme** | Indigo blue gradient, Google Fonts Inter, Material 3 |
| **Auth screens** | Glassmorphism cards on gradient background |
| **Home** | StreamBuilder for real-time updates, category/status filters |
| **Report cards** | Image thumbnails, color-coded status badges |
| **Admin Dashboard** | Real-time stat cards (Total/Pending/Resolved) |
| **Report Details** | SliverAppBar with hero image, info cards |
| **Animations** | Splash: fade + scale + elastic bounce |

---

## ⚙️ Android Permissions

Add to [android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml](file:///f:/Smart_Neighborhood_Reporting_App/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml) before `<application>`:

```xml
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET"/>
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION"/>
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION"/>
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.CAMERA"/>
```

Also ensure `minSdkVersion` is at least **21** in `android/app/build.gradle`.
